===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|Yangzi}} (ISO pinyin)

===Etymology===
An irregular transliteration from {{etyl|cmn|en}} {{zh-l|揚子江|tr=Yángzǐ Jiāng}}, an older Chinese name of the part of the river near [[Yangzhou]].

The folk etymology that it means "Son of the Ocean" derives from the homophonic [[misnomer]] [[洋]][[子]][[江]] which was apparently given to Matteo [[Ricci]], whose posthumously-published journals popularized the name in Europe as {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|Iansu}} and {{m|la|Iansuchian}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈjæŋ(t)si/|lang=en}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# The longest river in [[China]] that flows to the [[East China Sea]] north of [[Shanghai]].

